Fix $t\geqslant1$ and let $G$ be the GCD graph of Proposition ef{prop:Graph} with set of edges $\mathcal{E}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_t$ (where $\mathcal{E}_t$ is defined in Proposition ef{prop:GCD}), weight $\mu(v)=\psi(v)\varphi(v)/v$ and edge density $\delta$. If $\delta\ll 1/t$, then $\mu(\mathcal{E})\ll 1/t$ and so we are done. Therefore we may assume that \[ \delta\geqslant 1/t\quad	ext{and}\quad t>10^{2000}. \] Note that this implies that \[ t\geqslant 10\delta^{-1/50}. \] We apply Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges} to $G$ to find a GCD subgraph $G'=(\mu,\mathcal{V}',\mathcal{W}',\mathcal{E}',\mathcal{P}',f',g')$ of $G$ with edge density $\delta'$ satisfying either case ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case1} or ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case2} of its statement. In addition, we have that:  egin{enumerate} \item $\mathcal{R}(G')=\emptyset$; \item $\mu(\Gamma_{G'}(v))\geqslant(9\delta'/10)\mu(\mathcal{W}')$ for all $v\in\mathcal{V}'$; \item $\mu(\Gamma_{G'}(w))\geqslant(9\delta'/10)\mu(\mathcal{V}')$ for all $w\in\mathcal{W}'$. \end{enumerate} Set \[ a:=\prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'}p^{f'(p)} \quad	ext{and}\quad b:=\prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'}p^{g'(p)}. \] The definition of a GCD graph implies that \[ a|v\quad	ext{for all}\ v\in\mathcal{V}', \qquad b|w\quad 	ext{for all}\ w\in\mathcal{W}'. \] Moreover, since $\mathcal{R}(G')=\emptyset$, and $p^{\min\{f'(p),g'(p)\}}\|\gcd(v,w)$ for all $(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'$, we have that \[ \gcd(v,w)=\gcd(a,b) \quad	ext{for all}\quad(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'. \] Now, note that \[ \prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'}p^{|f'(p)-g'(p)|} = \prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'}p^{\max\{f'(p),g'(p)\}-\min\{f'(p),g'(p)\}}=  rac{\mathrm{lcm}(a,b)}{\gcd(a,b)} =  rac{ab}{\gcd(a,b)^2} , \] as well as \[ \prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'} rac{1}{(1-\mathds{1}_{f'(p)=g'(p)\geqslant1}/p)^2(1-1/p^{31/30})^{10}} \ll \prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'} rac{1}{(1-\mathds{1}_{f'(p)=g'(p)\geqslant1}/p)^2} \leqslant  rac{ab}{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)} . \] Consequently, from the definition of $q(\cdot)$, we find  egin{align} q(G') &= (\delta')^{10}\mu(\mathcal{V}')\mu(\mathcal{W}') \prod_{p\in\mathcal{P}'}  rac{p^{|f'(p)-g'(p)|}}{(1-\mathds{1}_{f'(p)=g'(p)\geqslant1}/p)^2(1-1/p^{31/30})^{10}}
onumber\ & \ll (\delta')^{10} \mu(\mathcal{V}')\mu(\mathcal{W}')  rac{ab}{\gcd(a,b)^2} \cdot  rac{ab}{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)}
onumber \ &= (\delta')^{9}\mu(\mathcal{E}')  rac{ab}{\gcd(a,b)^2} \cdot  rac{ab}{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)} . \end{align} Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges} offers a lower bound on $q(G')/q(G)$. Since \[ q(G) = \delta^{10} \mu(\mathcal{V})\mu(\mathcal{V})= \delta^{9}\mu(\mathcal{E}), \] we can obtain an upper bound on the size of $\mu(\mathcal{E})$ by estimating $q(G')$ from above. \medskip Note that \[ \mathcal{E}'\subseteq\mathcal{E} \subseteq\{(v,w)\in\mathcal{V}	imes\mathcal{V}: M(v,w)\leqslant t\cdot \gcd(v,w)\}, \] where we recall that $M(v,w)=\max\{v\psi(w),w\psi(v)\}$. Since $\gcd(v,w)=\gcd(a,b)$ for all $(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'$, we infer that \[ \psi(v)\leqslant  rac{t\cdot \gcd(a,b)}{w} \quad	ext{and}\quad \psi(w)\leqslant  rac{t\cdot \gcd(a,b)}{v} \quad	ext{for all}\quad (v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'. \] The vertex sets $\mathcal{V}',\mathcal{W}'$ are finite sets of positive integers. For each $v\in\mathcal{V}'$, let $w_{\max}(v)$ be the largest integer in $\mathcal{W}'$ such that $(v,w_{\max}(v))\in\mathcal{E}'$. (This quantity is well-defined in virtue of property (b) above. In addition, we emphasise to the reader that `largest' refers to the size of elements as positive integers, and does not depend on the measure $\mu$.) Similarly, for each $w\in\mathcal{W}'$, let $v_{\max}(w)$ be the largest element of $\mathcal{V}'$ such that $(v_{\max}(w),w)\in\mathcal{E}'$. Consequently,  egin{equation} \psi(v)\leqslant  rac{t\cdot \gcd(a,b)}{w_{\max}(v)} \quad	ext{and}\quad \psi(w)\leqslant  rac{t\cdot \gcd(a,b)}{v_{\max}(w)} \quad	ext{for all}\quad v\in \mathcal{V}',\,w\in\mathcal{W}'. \end{equation} Now, let $w_0$ be the largest integer in $\mathcal{W}'$ and $\mathcal{E}''=\{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}': (v,w_0)\in\mathcal{E}'\}$. We then have  egin{equation} w_{\max}(v)=w_0 \quad	ext{for all}\quad(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'' . \end{equation} In addition, since $G'$ satisfies conditions (b) and (c) in the statement of Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges}, we have \[ \mu(\mathcal{E}'') =\sum_{v\in \Gamma_{G'}(w_0)}\mu(v)\mu(\Gamma_{G'}(v)) \geqslant \mu(\Gamma_{G'}(w_0))\cdot  rac{9\delta'\mu(\mathcal{W}')}{10} \geqslant  igg( rac{9\delta'}{10} igg)^2 \mu(\mathcal{V}')\mu(\mathcal{W}')\geqslant  rac{\delta'\mu(\mathcal{E}')}{2} . \] Substituting this bound into \eqref{eq:QG'Bound}, we find  egin{equation} q(G') \ll (\delta')^{8} \mu(\mathcal{E}'')  rac{a b}{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)}\cdot  rac{a b}{\gcd(a,b)^2} \leqslant \mu(\mathcal{E}'')  rac{ab}{\gcd(a,b)^2} \cdot  rac{ab}{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)} . \end{equation} Here we used the trivial bound $\delta'\leqslant 1$ in the second inequality. In addition, \als{ \mu(\mathcal{E}'') = \sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}''}  rac{\psi(v)\varphi(v)}{v} \cdot  rac{\psi(w)\varphi(w)}{w} . } Since $a|v$ and $b|w$, we have $\varphi(v)/v\leqslant \varphi(a)/a$ and $\varphi(w)/w\leqslant \varphi(b)/b$. Therefore \[ \mu(\mathcal{E}'')\leqslant  rac{\varphi(a)\varphi(b)}{a b}\sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}''}\psi(v)\psi(w). \] Together with \eqref{psi ub}, \eqref{eq:w0} and \eqref{eq:q(G') bound}, this implies that  egin{equation} q(G') \ll t^2ab \sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}''}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(w) w_0} \leqslant t^2ab \sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(w) w_0} . \end{equation} We now split our argument depending on whether ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case1} or ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case2} of Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges} holds.  igskip 
oindent 	extit{Case 1: ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case1} of Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges} holds.} \medskip In this case we have $q(G')\gg \delta t^{50} q(G)$. Writing $v=v' a$ and $w=w' b$, we find that  egin{align*} \sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(w) w_0} &\leqslant \sum_{w'\leqslant w_0/b} rac{1}{ w_0 v_{\max}(b w')} \sum_{v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a}1\ &\leqslant \sum_{w'\leqslant w_0/b} rac{1}{ w_0 v_{\max}(b w')}\cdot  rac{v_{\max}(bw')}{a} \ &\leqslant  rac{1}{ab} . \end{align*} Together with \eqref{eq:G'Quality}, this implies that \[ q(G')\ll t^2. \] Since $q(G')\gg \delta t^{50} q(G)$ in this case, and since $\delta \geqslant 1/t$, this gives \[ \mu(\mathcal{E}) = \delta^{-9}q(G) \ll \delta^{-10}t^{-50}q(G')\ll  rac{1}{\delta^{10}t^{48}} \ll  rac{1}{t} . \] This establishes Proposition ef{prop:Graph} in this case.  igskip 
oindent 	extit{Case 2: ef{prop:Partd}-ef{prop:Case2} of Proposition ef{prop:BoundOnEdges} holds.} \medskip Write $v=v' a$ and $w=w' b$. In this case  egin{equation} L_t(v',w')\geqslant 4\quad	ext{whenever}\quad(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'. \end{equation} We also have $q(G')\gg q(G)$. From \eqref{eq:L_t-lowerbound}, we see that either \[ \sum_{p|v',\,p\geqslant t} rac{1}{p}\geqslant 2 \quad	ext{or} \quad \sum_{p|w',\,p\geqslant t} rac{1}{p}\geqslant 2 \] whenever $(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'$. Consequently, \als{ \sum_{(v,w)\in\mathcal{E}'}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(w) w_0} &\leqslant \mathop{\sum\sum}_{\substack{w'\leqslant w_0/b,\ v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a\ \sum_{p|v' w',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 4}}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(b w') w_0} \ &\leqslant S_1+S_2, } where  egin{align*} S_1&=\mathop{\sum\sum}_{\substack{w'\leqslant w_0/b,\ v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a\ \sum_{p|v',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 2}}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(b w') w_0} ,\ S_2&=\mathop{\sum\sum}_{\substack{w'\leqslant w_0/b,\ v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a\ \sum_{p|w',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 2}}  rac{1}{v_{\max}(b w') w_0} . \end{align*} For $S_1$, we note that \als{ S_1&\leqslant \sum_{w'\leqslant w_0/b}  rac{1}{w_0v_{\max}(b w')} \sum_{\substack{v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a \ \sum_{p|v',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 2}} 1\ &\ll \sum_{w'\leqslant w_0/b}  rac{1}{w_0v_{\max}(b w')} \cdot  rac{v_{\max}(b w')/a}{t^2e^t} \ &\leqslant  rac{1}{ab t^2e^t} } by Lemma ef{lem:Anatomy}, since $\exp(t^e)\gg\exp(t)t^2$. Similarly for $S_2$, we find that \als{ S_2&\leqslant\sum_{\substack{w'\leqslant w_0/b \ \sum_{p|w',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 2}}  rac{1}{w_0v_{\max}(b w')} \sum_{v'\leqslant v_{\max}(b w')/a}1\ &\leqslant \sum_{\substack{w'\leqslant w_0/b \ \sum_{p|w',\,p\geqslant t}1/p\geqslant 2}}  rac{1}{aw_0} \ &\ll  rac{1}{ab t^2e^t} , } by applying Lemma ef{lem:Anatomy} once again. Substituting these bounds into \eqref{eq:G'Quality}, we conclude that \[ q(G') \ll e^{-t}. \] Since we have $q(G)\ll q(G')$ and $\delta\geqslant 1/t$, this gives \[ \mu(\mathcal{E}) = \delta^{-9}q(G) \ll t^{9} q(G')\ll t^{9} e^{-t} \ll 1/t. \] This establishes Proposition ef{prop:Graph} in all cases.
